+
+# NAME
+
+io_uring_prep_waitid - prepare a waitid request
+
+# SYNOPSIS
+
+``` text
+#include <sys/wait.h>
+#include <liburing.h>
+
+ void io_uring_prep_waitid(struct io_uring_sqe * sqe ,
+                           idtype_t  idtype ,
+                           id_t  id ,
+                           siginfo_t * infop ,
+                           int  options ,
+                           unsigned int  flags );
+```
+
+# DESCRIPTION
+
+The **io_uring_prep_waitid**(3) function prepares a waitid request. The
+submission queue entry *sqe* is setup to use the *idtype* and *id*
+arguments select the child(ren), and *options* to specify the child
+state changes to wait for. Upon successful return, it fills *infop* with
+information of the child process, if any. *flags* is io_uring specific
+modifier flags. They are currently unused, and hence **0** should be
+passed.
+
+This function prepares an async **waitid**(2) request. See that man page
+for details.
