+header: liburing Manual
+section: 3
+title: io_uring_register_clock
+---
+
+# NAME
+
+io_uring_register_clock - set clock source for event waiting
+
+# SYNOPSIS
+
+``` text
+#include <liburing.h>
+
+ int io_uring_register_clock(struct io_uring * ring ,
+                             struct io_uring_clock_register * arg );
+```
+
+# DESCRIPTION
+
+The **io_uring_register_clock**(3) function registers which clock source
+should be used by io_uring, when an application waits for event
+completions. The *ring* argument should point to the ring in question,
+and the *arg* argument should be a pointer to a **struct
+io_uring_clock_register .**
+
+The *arg* argument must be filled in with the appropriate information.
+It looks as follows:
+
+``` text
+struct io_uring_clock_register {
+    __u32 clockid;
+    __u32 __resv[3];
+};
+```
+
+The *clockid* field must contain the clock source, with valid sources
+being:
+
+**CLOCK_MONOTONIC**
+
+: a nonsettable system-wide clock that represents monotonic time.
+
+**CLOCK_BOOTTIME**
+
+: A nonsettable system-wide clock that is identical to **CLOCK_MONOTONIC
+  ,** except that is also icnludes any time that the system is
+  suspended.
+
+See **clock_gettime**(3) for more details.
+
+The *\_\_resv* fields must be filled with zeroes.
+
+Available since 6.12.
+
+# RETURN VALUE
+
+On success **io_uring_register_clock**(3) returns 0. On failure it
+returns **-errno**.
+
+# SEE ALSO
+
+**clock_gettime**(3), **io_uring_register**(2),
+**io_uring_wait_cqe**(3), **io_uring_wait_cqe_timeout**(3),
