+.\" Copyright (C) 2021 Stefan Roesch <shr@fb.com>
+.\"
+.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.0-or-later
+.\"
+---
+date: November 15, 2021
+footer: liburing-2.1
+header: liburing Manual
+section: 3
+title: io_uring_wait_cqe
+---
+
+# NAME
+
+io_uring_wait_cqe - wait for one io_uring completion event
+
+# SYNOPSIS
+
+``` text
+#include <liburing.h>
+
+ int io_uring_wait_cqe(struct io_uring * ring ,
+                       struct io_uring_cqe ** cqe_ptr );
+```
+
+# DESCRIPTION
+
+The **io_uring_wait_cqe**(3) function waits for an IO completion from
+the queue belonging to the *ring* param, waiting for it if necessary. If
+an event is already available in the ring when invoked, no waiting will
+occur. The *cqe_ptr* param is filled in on success.
+
+After the caller has submitted a request with **io_uring_submit**(3),
+the application can retrieve the completion with
+**io_uring_wait_cqe**(3).
+
+# RETURN VALUE
+
+On success **io_uring_wait_cqe**(3) returns 0 and the cqe_ptr param is
+filled in. On failure it returns **-errno**. The return value indicates
+the result of waiting for a CQE, and it has no relation to the CQE
+result itself.
+
+# SEE ALSO
+
+**io_uring_submit**(3), **io_uring_wait_cqe_timeout**(3),
+**io_uring_wait_cqes**(3)
